 lips, and jawline remain consistent, and his original attire from <Picture 1> (cream ruffled shirt and dark burgundy velvet vest with ornate gold buttons and trim) is preserved unchanged.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 4], [Shot 5]): fully_preserved - her recognizable facial identity, blue-grey eyes, curly blonde hair with pearl ornaments, face-framing curls, eyebrows, porcelain complexion, and delicate proportions remain consistent, and her original attire from <Picture 2> (off-shoulder cream corset with lace trim, puffed lace sleeves, burgundy velvet skirt, and multi-strand pearl necklace) is preserved unchanged.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video uses restrained live-action romantic-drama cinematography with cool blue-hour ambience, warm practical lantern and ship lights, subtle 35mm film grain, shallow depth of field, and natural facial micro-expressions.\n\n[Shot 1] A long-lens wide shot establishes a nearly empty stone harbor quay at dusk in a historical European port. <Subject 1>, wearing his cream ruffled shirt and dark burgundy velvet vest with ornate gold buttons, carries a small leather travel satchel and stands near the gangplank of a sailing vessel on the right side of the composition. <Subject 2>, wearing her off-shoulder cream corset with lace trim, puffed lace sleeves, burgundy velvet skirt, and multi-strand pearl necklace, faces him several steps away on the left. A few figures in period dress move between them in soft focus while wind off the water lifts <Subject 2>'s loose curls and stirs the hem of her skirt and <Subject 1>'s ruffled cuffs. Neither immediately approaches. The camera pushes in with small amplitude at slow speed as lantern light flickers behind them and the ship's lamps glow.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:03.000, the camera cuts to a restrained medium two-shot from the side. The sailing vessel remains behind <Subject 1>, while <Subject 2> stands close enough to touch him but keeps her hands around the end of her pearl necklace. She looks at the gangplank and then back into his eyes. <Subject 2> (S1), speaking in a soft young female voice with a slight tremble and a measured pace, says: [English] I thought we'd have more time. She attempts a smile, but it fades before fully forming.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:06.000, the camera cuts to a close-up of <Subject 1>. Warm lantern light crosses one side of his face while the rest remains in cool evening shadow. His eyes lower, his jaw tightens briefly, and he gives a quiet breath through his nose. <Subject 1> (S2), speaking in a low young male voice with restrained regret, replies: [English] We did. We just spent it being afraid. His gaze returns to her, carrying apology without asking for forgiveness.\n\n[Shot 4] At 00:09.500, the camera cuts to an intimate close-up of <Subject 2>. Her blue-grey eyes become moist, but no tear falls. A passing traveler briefly obscures the frame; when the traveler clears, her expression has softened. <Subject 2> (S1) says with a steadier voice and the beginning of acceptance: [English] Then let's not be afraid of goodbye. She gives him a small, genuine smile.\n\n[Shot 5] At 00:12.500, the camera cuts back to a long-lens medium-wide shot. <Subject 1> reaches forward, and their fingertips meet briefly rather than forming an embrace. The ship's departure bell sounds. <Subject 2> gently releases his hand first. <Subject 1> steps backward onto the gangplank while maintaining eye contact. The vessel begins to pull away from the quay, widening the gap between them. End at exactly 00:15.000 with both characters giving the same restrained, accepting smile across the narrowing distance. Natural anatomy, stable identities, accurate English lip synchronization, no exaggerated crying, no dramatic embrace, no subtitles, no visible generated text, 16:9.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nCold harbor wind, distant water lapping the stone quay, the creak of wooden masts and rigging, rolling wheels of a wooden cart, footsteps on cobbles